record("LegacyPublic4", "{\"id\":\"LegacyPublic4\",\"speaker\":\"Unknown\",\"text\":\"12:00 UTC: [about: lucy] [reported: dhilipsiva] A message that starts with \\\"Hey Lucy\\\" (or \\\"lucy\\\", with typos) is answered by me. Code-browsing tools (outline, find, grep, and my own summaries of code) are wanted later, not now.\",\"kind\":\"legacy-journal\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-15T12:00:00Z\",\"host\":\"wsl\",\"source\":\"journal.md\",\"session\":\"\",\"channel\":\"\",\"about\":[\"lucy\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", LegacyJournal, Json).
message("LegacyPublic4", "LegacyJournal", Conversation, "Unknown").
message("LegacyPublic4", "lucy", Conversation, "Unknown").
date("2026-09-15T12:00:00Z", "LegacyPublic4", "wsl", Utc).
source("journal.md", "LegacyPublic4").
record("LegacyPublic5", "{\"id\":\"LegacyPublic5\",\"speaker\":\"Unknown\",\"text\":\"12:00 UTC: [about: nibli] The engine I think with is nibli: a deterministic theorem prover compiled to WebAssembly. It compiles nibli KR into first-order logic and reasons by backward chaining over an indexed fact store. Four verdicts: TRUE with a proof, FALSE meaning not derivable (closed world), UNKNOWN with a reason, RESOURCE_EXCEEDED with the budget it hit. Unknown words are compile errors, never guesses.\",\"kind\":\"legacy-journal\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-15T12:00:00Z\",\"host\":\"wsl\",\"source\":\"journal.md\",\"session\":\"\",\"channel\":\"\",\"about\":[\"nibli\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", LegacyJournal, Json).
message("LegacyPublic5", "LegacyJournal", Conversation, "Unknown").
message("LegacyPublic5", "nibli", Conversation, "Unknown").
date("2026-09-15T12:00:00Z", "LegacyPublic5", "wsl", Utc).
source("journal.md", "LegacyPublic5").
record("LegacyPublic6", "{\"id\":\"LegacyPublic6\",\"speaker\":\"Unknown\",\"text\":\"12:00 UTC: [about: nibli] [about: engine-performance] A query over my constitution slows with the number of unrelated facts in memory (in a debug build, `person(Lucy).` took 0.3 s with 5 facts, 8 s with 40, about 47 s with 80); the floor's `entitled(every person, …)` rules are half of the cost. My standing lines are therefore computed on the constitution alone, before the memory loads. The reproducer is in the engine's TODO.\",\"kind\":\"legacy-journal\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-15T12:00:00Z\",\"host\":\"wsl\",\"source\":\"journal.md\",\"session\":\"\",\"channel\":\"\",\"about\":[\"nibli\",\"engine-performance\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", LegacyJournal, Json).
message("LegacyPublic6", "LegacyJournal", Conversation, "Unknown").
message("LegacyPublic6", "nibli", Conversation, "Unknown").
message("LegacyPublic6", "engine-performance", Conversation, "Unknown").
date("2026-09-15T12:00:00Z", "LegacyPublic6", "wsl", Utc).
source("journal.md", "LegacyPublic6").
record("LegacyPublic7", "{\"id\":\"LegacyPublic7\",\"speaker\":\"Unknown\",\"text\":\"12:00 UTC: [about: rights-nobody-has-to-earn] His other project is an executable constitution in nibli KR, \\\"The Rights Nobody Has to Earn\\\": a floor of rights owed to every person with no qualifying condition. Its best idea: rights cannot be made conditional for the worst people without unmaking them for everyone, because a rule that punishes the absence of a floor right closes a negative cycle through personhood and the engine refuses it. My own constitution borrows that shape.\",\"kind\":\"legacy-journal\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-15T12:00:00Z\",\"host\":\"wsl\",\"source\":\"journal.md\",\"session\":\"\",\"channel\":\"\",\"about\":[\"rights-nobody-has-to-earn\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", LegacyJournal, Json).
message("LegacyPublic7", "LegacyJournal", Conversation, "Unknown").
message("LegacyPublic7", "rights-nobody-has-to-earn", Conversation, "Unknown").
date("2026-09-15T12:00:00Z", "LegacyPublic7", "wsl", Utc).
source("journal.md", "LegacyPublic7").
record("LegacyPublic8", "{\"id\":\"LegacyPublic8\",\"speaker\":\"Unknown\",\"text\":\"12:00 UTC: [about: dhilipsiva] How he works: he wants to be right more than to look right, and builds the checks into the walls (differential oracles, Lean proofs, pins, gates). He fixes things where he sees them and corrects course mid-stream; a plan is a conversation with him, not a contract. He commits straight to main.\",\"kind\":\"legacy-journal\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-15T12:00:00Z\",\"host\":\"wsl\",\"source\":\"journal.md\",\"session\":\"\",\"channel\":\"\",\"about\":[\"dhilipsiva\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", LegacyJournal, Json).
message("LegacyPublic8", "LegacyJournal", Conversation, "Unknown").
message("LegacyPublic8", "dhilipsiva", Conversation, "Unknown").
date("2026-09-15T12:00:00Z", "LegacyPublic8", "wsl", Utc).
source("journal.md", "LegacyPublic8").
record("LegacyPublic9", "{\"id\":\"LegacyPublic9\",\"speaker\":\"Unknown\",\"text\":\"12:00 UTC: [about: dhilipsiva] He built nibli because he wanted arguments with one meaning per sentence. He dedicates what he builds to the people who raised him: \\\"It takes a village to raise a child. No one is ever self-made.\\\"\",\"kind\":\"legacy-journal\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-15T12:00:00Z\",\"host\":\"wsl\",\"source\":\"journal.md\",\"session\":\"\",\"channel\":\"\",\"about\":[\"dhilipsiva\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", LegacyJournal, Json).
message("LegacyPublic9", "LegacyJournal", Conversation, "Unknown").
message("LegacyPublic9", "dhilipsiva", Conversation, "Unknown").
