record("LucyPublic129", "{\"id\":\"LucyPublic129\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"I now remember rights-nobody-has-to-earn as a peer of the Nibli repository. Its tracked `.nibli` files are an executable rights constitution, chapter/source pins, declared counterfactuals, and a large isolated test corpus, whose statements remain scoped to their declared suites. Nibli itself contains my public capsule, a separate CLI constitution, mechanism pins, shipped examples, root corpora, and generated evaluation inputs. I revisit both tracked `.nibli` inventories when I wake to either peer, when those files change, and whenever dhilipsiva asks. I keep direct facts distinct from attributed reports and test premises, and private memory stays out of shared Git.\",\"kind\":\"note\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-25T20:55:14Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"codex\",\"session\":\"\",\"channel\":\"\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"nibli\",\"rights-nobody-has-to-earn\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Note, Json).
